This suite must be recorded and re-checked on a database with no history.

Five batch-2 cases print values that are a function of how many objects the
instance has ever created, not of what the case did:

  pdt/Design/CREATE_INDEX/LOCAL/RangePartTable.sql   __SYS_PART_IDX_ID_<n>
  pdt/Design/CREATE_INDEX/LOCAL/HashPartTable.sql    __SYS_PART_IDX_ID_<n>
  pdt/Design/CREATE_INDEX/LOCAL/ListPartTable.sql    __SYS_PART_IDX_ID_<n>
  pdt/Design/CREATE_TABLE/AS_SELECT/RangePartTable.sql  SYS_PART_TABLES_.TABLE_ID
  pdt/Design/DELETE/RangePartTable.sql               which FK is reported first

They came that way from the original suite, which never noticed because ATAF's
auto-init recreates the database on every run. natc-check.sh keeps auto-init
OFF on purpose (it would destroy the isolated instance), so it reads this file
instead and recreates the instance itself. The other 110 wired cases are
byte-identical back to back on a database that already has history.

See docs/analysis/claude-global-index/v4-natc-port.md 6.
